  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Evaluate $\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061(-\\operatorname{ln}\u20614).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061(-\\operatorname{ln}\u20614)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061x$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061x & =\\frac{{e}^{x}-{e}^{-x}}{{e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}-1}{{e}^{2x}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2x}}{1+{e}^{-2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the third definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061(-\\operatorname{ln}\u20614) & =\\frac{1-{e}^{-2(-\\operatorname{ln}\u20614)}}{1+{e}^{-2(-\\operatorname{ln}\u20614)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}}{1+{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}\u20614}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{4}^{2}}}{1+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u206116}}{1+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u206116}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-16}{1+16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
